<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia's net foreign reserves hit new high.</title>
<headline>Colombia's net foreign reserves hit new high.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's net foreign reserves rose $11.5 million to a new historic high of $10.23 billion in the week ending June 6, the latest date for which official figures are available, the central bank said.</p>
<p>It said net reserves grew by $335 million between Jan. 1 and June 6 against targeted growth for the entire year of about $750 million.</p>
<p>((-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
